  "_key": "!scenes!e9d1497b54cb4234",
  "description": "<p><strong>Daytime.</strong> Where the players may try to take Euphoria as she crosses the pavement to a waiting vehicle. The book prints no exterior map — this one is original and carries no authority, so resize or replace it freely.</p><p>Knight Errant maintain a detail on the door; the guard inside can hit the PANICBUTTON, and <strong>four Lone Star officers arrive in five minutes</strong> (QE p.14). A car at the kerb with the engine running is the difference between a snatch and a firefight.</p><p><strong>Rooms:</strong> Ward Street frontage: the tower's four sets of double doors under a covered drop-off, kerb and bollards, the carriageway, the far pavement with an alley mouth, and the waterfront promenade along the west flank.</p><p><em><strong>GM-invented layout.</strong> The adventure plays scenes at this location but prints no floorplan for it, so nothing here carries the book's authority. Resize or replace freely.</em></p>"
